<title>USA: LONG UPS STRIKE BAD FOR US ECONOMY--FED'S PHILLIPS.</title>
<headline>LONG UPS STRIKE BAD FOR US ECONOMY--FED'S PHILLIPS.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>A prolonged strike at United Parcel Service (UPS), the nation's largest package delivery company, could have negative effects on the U.S. economy, Federal Reserve governor Susan Phillips said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;If it goes on for a long time we'll start to see some economic impact,&quot; Phillips told Reuters in an interview.</p>
<p>However, she added: &quot;I'm not too worried at this point.&quot;</p>
<p>The Teamsters union and UPS management resumed negotiations on Thursday but there were few signs that the stoppage would end soon.</p>
<p>((--Washington newsroom, 202 898-8377))</p>
